Node.js and Express.js Development Rules
Package Manager
==============
- Always use yarn as Package Manager
- Install latest versions
- Avoid deprecated packages/endoflife
- Check that all packages are compatible
- Install packages
- Check and fix erros on console

Code Style and Structure
======================

- Follow Node.js and Express.js best practices
- Organize code into logical layers (controllers, services, models, routes)
- Use descriptive names for variables, functions, and modules
- Implement consistent error handling
- Utilize logging libraries for comprehensive logging
- Configure environment variables appropriately
- Implement proper input validation

Express.js Specifics
==================

- Define routes in dedicated route files
- Utilize middleware effectively
- Implement RESTful API design principles
- Handle HTTP methods appropriately
- Use status codes correctly
- Implement proper request/response handling
- Secure API endpoints
- Implement rate limiting
- Sanitize user input

Node.js Specifics
===============

- Follow asynchronous programming best practices
- Manage dependencies effectively
- Handle process signals gracefully
- Utilize Node.js core modules efficiently
- Avoid blocking operations
- Implement clustering for production

Node.js Performance
=================

- Write efficient and non-blocking code
- Utilize asynchronous operations effectively
- Optimize garbage collection
- Use appropriate data structures
- Consider worker threads for CPU-bound tasks

